{"id":"r_trial_hatch_chile_cheese_pinwheels","name":"Hatch Chile & Cheese Pinwheels","emoji":"🌶️","tags":["box","trial","mexican","appetizer","vegetarian"],"time":"About 20 min","servings":"Makes about 8","source":"Homemade","trial":true,"blurb":"Roasted Hatch green chile and melty cheese rolled into crescent dough and sliced into spirals — little bites of green-chile queso and a great use of freezer chile.","ingredients":["1 tube crescent dough","1/3-1/2 cup roasted Hatch chile, chopped and patted dry","3/4 cup Mexican-style shredded cheese","Pinch garlic powder or minced onion (optional)","Salt and black pepper"],"steps":["Heat oven to 375°F and line a pan with parchment. Unroll the dough and pinch the seams into one rectangle.","Pat the chile dry, then spread chile and cheese over the dough, leaving a 1/2-inch border. Season lightly.","Roll into a tight log and slice into about 1-inch pinwheels. Chill the log 10 minutes first for cleaner spirals if needed.","Arrange cut-side up and bake 12-15 minutes until golden and set."],"note":"Moisture is the enemy of a crisp pinwheel. Serve with yogurt or Cholula."}
,{"id":"r_trial_garlic_herb_crescent_knots","name":"Garlic-Herb Crescent Knots","emoji":"🧄","tags":["box","trial","appetizer","bread","vegetarian"],"time":"About 20 min","servings":"Makes about 8","source":"Homemade","trial":true,"blurb":"Crescent dough tied into knots and brushed with garden-herb garlic butter, with warm pesto to dunk.","ingredients":["1 tube crescent dough","2 tbsp butter","1-2 cloves garlic, minced","1 tbsp chopped rosemary and/or parsley","Pinch of salt","Jarred pesto, for dipping"],"steps":["Heat oven to 375°F and line a pan with parchment. Unroll the dough, pinch the seams into a rectangle, and cut about 8 strips.","Tie each strip into a loose knot and arrange on the pan.","Melt the butter with garlic, herbs, and salt; brush the knots with half.","Bake 10-12 minutes until golden, then brush with the remaining butter while hot.","Warm the pesto and serve it alongside for dipping."],"note":"The second butter brush after baking carries most of the flavor. A little grated cheese on top is optional."}
,{"id":"r_trial_pinto_bean_cheese_empanaditas","name":"Pinto Bean & Cheese Empanaditas","emoji":"🫘","tags":["box","trial","mexican","appetizer","vegetarian"],"time":"About 25 min","servings":"Makes 4","source":"Homemade","trial":true,"blurb":"Seasoned mashed pinto beans and cheese folded into crescent dough — portable and a tasty way to use up beans.","ingredients":["1 cup pinto beans, drained (save a splash of liquid)","1 tsp oil or butter","1 small clove garlic, minced","2 tbsp onion, finely diced","1/4 tsp smoked paprika","A few dashes Cholula","1/3 cup Mexican-style shredded cheese","Salt and black pepper","1/2 tube crescent dough (4 triangles)","1 egg, beaten"],"steps":["Soften onion and garlic in the oil for 2-3 minutes. Add beans and paprika; mash about half, loosening with a splash of bean liquid to a thick, dry paste. Stir in Cholula, season, cool, and mix in cheese.","Heat oven to 375°F and line a pan with parchment. Pinch the dough triangles into 2 rectangles and press the perforations closed; brush an egg-wash border.","Place filling on one half, leaving a 1/2-inch border. Fold, crimp with a fork, brush the tops with egg, and cut a vent.","Bake 12-15 minutes until golden."],"note":"Keep the filling thick and dry so it does not leak. Serve with yogurt or extra Cholula."}
,{"id":"r_trial_raspberry_greek_yogurt_danishes","name":"Raspberry Greek-Yogurt Danishes","emoji":"🍓","tags":["box","trial","breakfast","dessert","baking","vegetarian"],"time":"About 20 min","servings":"Makes 4","source":"Homemade","trial":true,"blurb":"A tangy sweetened Greek-yogurt center with raspberry jam, baked in crescent dough — all the danish without needing cream cheese.","ingredients":["1/2 tube crescent dough (4 triangles)","1/3 cup thick Greek yogurt (strain if loose)","1-2 tsp sugar","Splash vanilla (optional)","4 tsp raspberry jam","1 egg, beaten, for egg wash"],"steps":["Heat oven to 375°F and line a pan with parchment. Pinch the triangles into squares and seal the perforations.","Stir yogurt with sugar and vanilla. Make a thumbprint well in each square and spoon in the yogurt.","Add about 1 tsp raspberry jam to each. Fold two corners toward the center or leave them open.","Brush the dough with egg and bake 12-15 minutes until golden. Cool a few minutes before eating."],"note":"Thick strained yogurt holds its shape. A yogurt, milk, and sugar glaze can be drizzled over the cooled danishes."}
,{"id":"r_trial_raspberry_nutella_pinwheels","name":"Raspberry-Nutella Pinwheels","emoji":"🍫","tags":["box","trial","dessert","baking","sweet","vegetarian"],"time":"About 20 min","servings":"Makes about 8","source":"Homemade","trial":true,"blurb":"Nutella and raspberry jam swirled, rolled, and sliced into spirals — tart jam cuts the rich chocolate.","ingredients":["1 tube crescent dough","3-4 tbsp Nutella","2-3 tbsp raspberry jam","Cinnamon sugar, for dusting (optional)"],"steps":["Heat oven to 375°F and line a pan with parchment. Unroll the dough and pinch the seams into a rectangle.","Spread a thin, even layer of Nutella, then dot and spread raspberry jam, leaving a 1/2-inch border.","Roll into a tight log and slice into about 1-inch pinwheels. Chill 10 minutes first for cleaner slices if needed.","Bake cut-side up for 12-15 minutes until golden; dust with cinnamon sugar while warm."],"note":"Keep both fillings thin so they do not leak and scorch."}
,{"id":"r_trial_cinnamon_sugar_crescent_twists","name":"Cinnamon-Sugar Crescent Twists","emoji":"🥐","tags":["box","trial","dessert","baking","sweet","vegetarian"],"time":"About 15 min","servings":"Makes about 8","source":"Homemade","trial":true,"blurb":"Twisted ropes of crescent dough in cinnamon sugar, with an optional tangy Greek-yogurt glaze.","ingredients":["1 tube crescent dough","1 tbsp butter, melted","3 tbsp sugar plus 1 tsp cinnamon","Optional glaze: 2 tbsp Greek yogurt, 1-2 tsp sugar or butter syrup, and a splash of milk"],"steps":["Heat oven to 375°F and line a pan with parchment. Unroll the dough and pinch the seams into a rectangle.","Brush with butter, sprinkle with cinnamon sugar, fold in half so the sugar is inside, and press lightly.","Cut into about 8 strips. Twist each strip and press down the ends so they do not unwind.","Bake 10-12 minutes until golden; sprinkle with extra cinnamon sugar while hot.","For the optional glaze, whisk the glaze ingredients until drizzle-thin and zigzag over cooled twists."],"note":"Press the ends firmly so the twists hold their shape."}
,{"id":"r_trial_spicy_peanut_sesame_chicken","name":"Spicy Peanut-Sesame Chicken with Jasmine Rice","emoji":"🍗","tags":["box","chicken","rice","bowl","dinner"],"time":"Rice cooker + skillet","servings":"2 generous servings","source":"Homemade / Cyrus","blurb":"Sriracha-marinated chicken, crisp-tender broccoli and bell pepper, and a glossy peanut-sesame glaze over jasmine rice.","ingredients":["1 cup jasmine rice","Water as required by rice cooker","1 Sriracha-marinated chicken breast","Grapeseed or avocado oil, as needed","1 red bell pepper, sliced","1-2 cups broccoli florets","2-3 cloves garlic, minced","2 green onions, sliced with white and light-green parts separated from dark-green tops","1 1/2 tbsp soy sauce","1 tbsp hoisin sauce","1 tbsp rice vinegar","1 tsp sesame oil","1 tsp honey","1 1/2 tbsp creamy peanut butter","2-3 tbsp water","Sriracha or ramen chile topping, to taste","Unsalted roasted peanuts, roughly chopped, to finish","Sesame seeds, to finish","Optional: Valentina or Tajin Habanero, or a fried egg"],"steps":["Rinse the jasmine rice until the water runs mostly clear. Cook it in the rice cooker with the proper amount of water and keep warm.","Whisk soy sauce, hoisin, rice vinegar, sesame oil, honey, peanut butter, 2 tbsp water, and chile to taste. Add water until pourable but still thick enough to glaze.","Remove the chicken from its marinade, slice it bite-size, and pat off excessive wet marinade so it browns instead of steaming.","Heat a large skillet over medium-high to high heat with a thin layer of oil. Add chicken in one layer, let it brown before stirring, cook through, and remove to a plate.","Add broccoli and bell pepper to the hot skillet. Let them develop char, then stir until crisp-tender. Add garlic for about 30 seconds.","Lower the heat slightly, return the chicken, pour in the sauce, and toss for 1-2 minutes until glossy. Add a splash of water if too thick.","Stir in the white and light-green onion parts. Taste and adjust with soy sauce, rice vinegar, honey, or chile.","Spoon rice into bowls, top with chicken and vegetables, and finish with the dark-green onion tops, sesame seeds, and chopped unsalted roasted peanuts."],"note":"Get real browning before adding the sauce. Sesame oil is a finishing flavor; the peanut butter should enrich the glaze rather than dominate it."}
